Repair only the supplied scientific or grammatical issues. Return {sections:[{id:number,patches:[{before:string,after:string,issueIndex:number}],reason:string}]}. Include each supplied section exactly once. Use exact unique substrings in its candidate. At most 3 non-overlapping patches per section; their combined BEFORE text must cover at most 35% of that section. issueIndex refers to that section's issues. Keep wording elsewhere unchanged. Restore the original meaning, uncertainty and proposal status. No extra style pass. If bounded repairs cannot solve the issues, return patches:[] and explain.
INPUT DATA:
{"sections": [{"id": 3, "heading": "Methodology", "original": "We will apply the fixed timetable and holding policy to arrivals from 18 weekdays [S2]. Each simulated decision will use only information available at that point in the log. Peak and off-peak periods will remain separate throughout analysis. We will preserve instances of service disruption, since removing difficult days could make the policy appear more dependable than it is.", "candidate": "We will apply the fixed timetable and holding policy to arrivals from 18 weekdays [S2]. Each simulated decision will use only information available at that point in the log. Peak and off-peak periods will be analyzed separately. We will retain instances of service disruption to ensure the policy's reliability is accurately reflected.", "issues": [{"originalQuote": "We will preserve instances of service disruption, since removing difficult days could make the policy appear more dependable than it is.", "revisedQuote": "We will retain instances of service disruption to ensure the policy's reliability is accurately reflected.", "problem": "Retaining disruptions helps avoid an overly favourable assessment but cannot ensure accurate reliability estimates. The revision replaces a qualified bias concern with an unsupported guarantee."}]}, {"id": 4, "heading": "Planned Evaluation", "original": "The planned measures are mean waiting time, the frequency of long waits and the difference between peak and off-peak outcomes. We will report days on which the holding policy performs worse as well as those on which it improves the average. Sensitivity checks will vary the definition of a long wait without selecting the definition that most favours either policy.", "candidate": "The planned measures include mean waiting time, the frequency of long waits, and the difference between peak and off-peak outcomes. We will report days when the holding policy performs worse, as well as those where it improves the average. Sensitivity checks will vary the definition of a long wait without favoring either policy.", "issues": [{"originalQuote": "Sensitivity checks will vary the definition of a long wait without selecting the definition that most favours either policy.", "revisedQuote": "Sensitivity checks will vary the definition of a long wait without favoring either policy.", "problem": "The revision loses the explicit commitment against selecting whichever long-wait definition most favours a policy. A general statement of impartiality does not preserve this methodological safeguard."}]}], "sources": [{"id": "S1", "title": "Controlled source packet: domain and evidence brief", "excerpt": "The proposed transport study uses an anonymized bus arrival log from one route. The log contains scheduled and observed arrivals but no passenger identities. Its coverage is limited to weekdays. A lower mean waiting time does not imply that every passenger group benefits.", "content_kind": "author_constructed_evaluation_fixture"}, {"id": "S2", "title": "Controlled source packet: experimental design brief", "excerpt": "The team will compare a fixed timetable with a holding policy using the same recorded arrivals. Peak and off-peak periods will be reported separately. The analysis will use 18 weekdays and will not make a causal claim about passenger satisfaction.", "content_kind": "author_constructed_evaluation_fixture"}]}
